From: Vyron Code D-11 local hardening (VYRON_CODE_D11_PATCH_0004_FINAL_LOG_PRIVACY_COMPLETION)
Applies to: NousResearch/hermes-agent, installed local copy, version 0.21.0, ON TOP OF patches
0001 and 0002 (both must already be applied; verified present 2026-09-24).

NOT APPLIED BY THIS TOOLING. This file was generated from `diff -u` of the real installed source
against a patched copy, every edited file was parsed as valid Python, the two behavioural pieces
(hermes_logging.py record factory, stream_diag.py) were exercised in isolation with the patched
copies, and `git apply --check` was run against the real installed Hermes root. Nothing was
written to the installed source. The user applies it manually.

PATCH 0003 IS OBSOLETE. Do not apply it. Its three hunks (turn_context.py, turn_recovery.py x2)
are already present in the installed source through patch 0002 (with the placeholder
"<redacted:persist_disabled>"), so 0003 no longer applies (`git apply --check` fails on it).

WHAT REMAINS AFTER 0001 + 0002 (live-proven 2026-09-24 with three fresh markers):
  1. `agent/chat_completion_helpers.py` logs the raw provider error text plus a full traceback
     ("Streaming failed before delivery") to agent.log AND errors.log on every failed request.
  2. The `[api-...]` session tag is stamped on log lines by a global LogRecord factory in
     `hermes_logging.py` (thread-local set by `set_session_context()`), and the session ID also
     appears inside message text; the tag even lingers on the thread after a request ends.
  3. Other error-path log lines that carry error text or request-derived counts: the
     stream-retry/exhausted diagnostics (`agent/stream_diag.py`), "Retrying API call ... error=",
     "API call failed after N retries ... msgs= tokens=", and the Codex error line.
  4. The aiohttp access log line records the response size (response-derived metadata).
  5. SUCCESS-PATH lines (found by reading a real successful turn in the existing log): "API call #N"
     logs prompt/completion/total token counts, cache stats and the provider response id
     (`agent/turn_usage.py`), and "Turn ended" logs `response_len=` (`agent/turn_finalizer.py`).

WHAT THIS PATCH CHANGES (13 hunks, 8 files; every hunk carries the marker VYRON_LOCAL_PATCH_0004):
  hermes_logging.py                       (2 hunks) ephemeral-session registry + record factory
  agent/turn_context.py                   (2 hunks) flag the session ephemeral; history count
  agent/chat_completion_helpers.py        (2 hunks) lines ~3404 and ~3433 stream error logs
  agent/stream_diag.py                    (1 hunk)  log_stream_retry() - the single choke point
  agent/turn_recovery.py                  (3 hunks) retries-exhausted, retrying, Codex error
  agent/turn_finalizer.py                 (1 hunk)  "Turn ended" line: response_len (success path)
  agent/turn_usage.py                     (1 hunk)  "API call #N" line: tokens/cache/id (success path)
  gateway/platforms/api_server.py         (1 hunk)  aiohttp access-log format

  Scope: every guard is conditional on `agent._persist_disabled` (set only by patch 0001, i.e.
  only for API Server agents) or on the in-memory ephemeral-session registry. A normal Hermes
  agent (CLI, TUI, gateway platforms, desktop) has `_persist_disabled == False`, so it keeps its
  original session tag, its full tracebacks and every original diagnostic line, unchanged. The
  only non-agent-scoped change is the aiohttp access-log format; it is safe here because every
  agent this API Server creates is persistence-disabled (patch 0001), and it keeps method, path
  and status. Drop that one hunk if you serve non-ephemeral clients from the same API Server.

  Nothing is deleted after writing, no new file/database/cache is created (the registry is a
  bounded in-memory dict, max 4096 IDs), and logging is not disabled: ephemeral agents still log
  severity, category (exception class name), retry count, elapsed time, provider/model names and
  HTTP status.

